<title>USA: MBIA qualifies eight muni issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies eight muni issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Insurance Corp said Thursday it qualified for bond insurance the following eight municipal issues set for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Hobart Park and Recreation District, Ind., $3.8 million improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Malta School District No 14, Mont., $2 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Hudson County, N.J., $9.14 million GO school bonds.</p>
<p>--Hudson County, N.J., $3.325 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Hudson County, N.J., $39.185 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Palmyra, N.J., 43.395 million improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Miller Place Union Free School District, N.Y., $8.43 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Albany, Ore., $3.7 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
